# Windows More tools menu duplicates hosted apps also present in the local MCP catalog

## Reproduction

On Windows, with a hosted app thread entrypoint also present in the local `codex_apps` MCP catalog, open a Codex conversation, then its right-panel New tab menu → More tools → Plugins and MCPs.

The menu shows this order:

1. Parts Tray
2. Example panel
3. Parts Tray
4. OpenAI Developers
5. Example panel

Both duplicated private-app choices open separate tabs; the first rendered its expected page. Reproduced twice. Private app labels and tool names below are replaced with synthetic examples. No screenshot, account IDs, installed plugin IDs, local paths, or rendered app content is included.

The local cached MCP catalog contains exactly one registration each for the three thread tools shown in this menu. Bits & Bolts Remote has one installed plugin entry and one local installation marker. Personal and workspace plugin-directory listings have the same plugin IDs, rather than separate installations.


## Installed build

Platform: Windows x64. Subscription details omitted for privacy.

- Windows package: `OpenAI.Codex_26.1002.7124.0_x64__2p2nqsd0c76g0`.
- App update tool reports app version `26.1002.52244`, build `13536`, release channel `prod`.
- Update eligibility could not be established: the Windows Store check returned unavailable because it may require a download.

## Static root-cause evidence

Read-only inspection of the installed renderer, `webview/assets/app-initial-25361a10f2bf.js`, identifies selector `jvs` around character offset `8564275`. It concatenates the hosted thread-entrypoint selector with the local MCP thread-entrypoint selector:

```js
[
  ...get(zvn, { hostId: durableHost, productContext: "codex" }),
  ...get(rk, localHost).filter(view => view.entrypoint.type === "thread")
]
```

It then filters enablement and handles code review, but never deduplicates the combined list. `jt` in `thread-side-panel-new-tab-1a88b1c55634.js` renders every resulting view as a menu item.

The hosted selector `k_n` already deduplicates its own input by `[appId, toolName]`. Local metadata matching `J_n`/`Y_n`, and identity helper `K_n`, already normalize `codex_apps` tools using the connector ID and canonical action name from `_meta._codex_apps.resource_uri`, parsed by `Vse`/`zH`/`Xmn`. For example, a synthetic namespaced local tool `example.open_panel` has canonical action name `open_panel`.

This code permits the exact duplicated menu when the same app tool appears in both sources. The observed order fits two hosted items followed by three local items. Hosted runtime rows were not captured, so that specific source assignment remains inference rather than a runtime trace.

## Proposed fix and verification

Deduplicate the permitted combined list by canonical app ID, action/tool name, and entrypoint type, retaining the first hosted view. Preserve standalone MCP entries using a fallback identity containing host, server, and tool name. Do not deduplicate by title or strip namespace prefixes.

Verification evaluates the exact extracted selector expression with local metadata shapes and inferred hosted descriptors. The original returns the observed five labels; the proposed patch returns three. All six checks pass, including preserving distinct tools with identical titles, standalone MCP servers, the ChatGPT route, and permitted local fallbacks when hosted rows are denied. Independent review found no actionable defects. This is an isolated selector test, not a live patched-app test.

Change the selector's return from:

```js
{ views: i.filter(e => get(wvn, e) === true), isPending: a }
```

to:

```js
{ views: uniqueThreadViews(i.filter(e => get(wvn, e) === true)), isPending: a }
```

The helper below uses the existing `Vse` canonical-identity parser:

```js
function threadViewKey(view) {
  if ("appId" in view) {
    return JSON.stringify(["app", view.appId, view.toolName, "thread"]);
  }
  const identity = view.server === "codex_apps" ? Vse(view.tool) : null;
  if (identity != null) {
    return JSON.stringify([
      "app", identity.connectorId, identity.actionName, view.entrypoint.type,
    ]);
  }
  return JSON.stringify([
    "mcp", view.hostId, view.server, view.tool.name, view.entrypoint.type,
  ]);
}

function uniqueThreadViews(views) {
  const seen = new Set();
  return views.filter(view => {
    const key = threadViewKey(view);
    if (seen.has(key)) return false;
    seen.add(key);
    return true;
  });
}
```

Applying this after enablement filtering preserves a permitted local entry when the matching hosted entry is unavailable.

The private app has a single `{type: "thread"}` declaration, which follows the official extension specification. Removing it would remove the intended menu entry. No installed package, plugin, connection, or cache was modified during this investigation.

Related report: https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/50757 also mentions duplicates in this Windows menu, although its main issue is empty required tool arguments and it does not establish the duplication's root cause.

## Self-contained reproduction and regression checks

Save the following as `menu-dedup.test.mjs` and run `node menu-dedup.test.mjs`. All app IDs, link IDs, and tool names in its fixtures are synthetic. The selector expression is copied from the installed renderer; dependencies are stubbed. Hosted fixture rows remain inferred. The standalone helper reproduces the existing URI parser; the integrated fix above should reuse `Vse`.

```js
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import vm from 'node:vm';

function threadViewKey(view) {
  if ('appId' in view) {
    return JSON.stringify(['app', view.appId, view.toolName, 'thread']);
  }
  if (view.server === 'codex_apps') {
    const parts = view.tool?._meta?._codex_apps?.resource_uri?.split('/');
    if (parts?.length === 4 && parts[0] === '' && parts.slice(1).every(Boolean)) {
      return JSON.stringify(['app', parts[1], parts[3], view.entrypoint.type]);
    }
  }
  return JSON.stringify(['mcp', view.hostId, view.server, view.tool.name, view.entrypoint.type]);
}

function uniqueThreadViews(views) {
  const seen = new Set();
  return views.filter(view => {
    const key = threadViewKey(view);
    if (seen.has(key)) return false;
    seen.add(key);
    return true;
  });
}

const evidence = {"jvsExpression": "Di(Hl,(e,{get:t,scope:n})=>{let r=n.value.routeKind===`chatgpt-thread`||e===`local`||e===`durable`?iGe:ag,i=[...t(zvn,{hostId:r,productContext:n.value.routeKind===`chatgpt-thread`?`chatgpt`:`codex`}),...n.value.routeKind===`chatgpt-thread`?[]:t(rk,e).filter(e=>e.entrypoint.type===`thread`)],a=n.value.routeKind!==`chatgpt-thread`&&t(tk)&&QO(e)===`app-server`&&t(lc,e).isPending,o=t(VOa);return i=[...i.filter(e=>e.server!==`code-review`),...o==null?[]:[o]],{views:i.filter(e=>t(wvn,e)===!0),isPending:a}})"};
const syntheticLocal = [
  {
    "name": "example.open_panel",
    "title": "Example panel",
    "connectorId": "sample-panel",
    "entrypoints": [
      {
        "type": "thread"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "developer.open_dashboard",
    "title": "OpenAI Developers",
    "connectorId": "sample-dev",
    "entrypoints": [
      {
        "type": "global"
      },
      {
        "type": "thread"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "parts.cad.tray",
    "title": "Parts Tray",
    "connectorId": "sample-parts",
    "entrypoints": [
      {
        "type": "thread"
      }
    ]
  }
];

// Synthetic names preserve the observed namespaced/canonical identity relationship.
const canonicalActions = {
  'example.open_panel': 'open_panel',
  'parts.cad.tray': 'cad.tray',
  'developer.open_dashboard': 'open_dashboard',
};
// Fixtures reproduce the observed menu ordering; all identities are synthetic.
const localOrder = ['parts.cad.tray', 'developer.open_dashboard',
  'example.open_panel'];
const local = localOrder.map(name => syntheticLocal.find(tool => tool.name === name))
  .flatMap(tool => tool.entrypoints.map(entrypoint => ({
  hostId: 'local', server: 'codex_apps', title: tool.title, entrypoint,
  tool: {name: tool.name, _meta: {_codex_apps: {
    resource_uri: `/${tool.connectorId}/redacted-link/${canonicalActions[tool.name]}`,
  }}},
})));
// Hosted descriptors are inferred fixtures, not captured live hosted state.
const hosted = ['parts.cad.tray', 'example.open_panel'].map(name => {
  const tool = syntheticLocal.find(tool => tool.name === name);
  return {appId: tool.connectorId, toolName: canonicalActions[name],
    server: tool.connectorId, hostId: 'durable', title: tool.title};
});

function evaluate(expression, {route = 'local-thread', hostedViews = hosted, localViews = local,
  permitted = () => true} = {}) {
  const context = vm.createContext({
    Di: (_scope, selector) => selector,
    Hl: 'Hl', iGe: 'durable', ag: 'local', zvn: 'hosted', rk: 'local',
    tk: 'enabled', lc: 'inventory', VOa: 'review', wvn: 'permission',
    QO: () => 'app-server', uniqueThreadViews,
  });
  const selector = vm.runInContext(expression, context);
  const result = selector('local', {
    scope: {value: {routeKind: route}},
    get: (source, value) => {
      switch (source) {
        case 'hosted': return hostedViews;
        case 'local': return localViews;
        case 'enabled': return true;
        case 'inventory': return {isPending: false};
        case 'review': return null;
        case 'permission': return permitted(value);
        default: throw new Error(`Unexpected selector input: ${source}`);
      }
    },
  });
  return Array.from(result.views);
}

const original = evidence.jvsExpression;
const before = 'views:i.filter(e=>t(wvn,e)===!0)';
assert.equal(original.split(before).length, 2, 'Patch target must occur exactly once');
const patched = original.replace(before, 'views:uniqueThreadViews(i.filter(e=>t(wvn,e)===!0))');
const originalViews = evaluate(original);
assert.deepEqual(originalViews.map(view => view.title),
  ['Parts Tray', 'Example panel', 'Parts Tray', 'OpenAI Developers', 'Example panel']);
assert.throws(() => assert.equal(originalViews.length, 3), assert.AssertionError);
console.log('RED reproduced: original selector returns five rows for three canonical tools.');

const fixed = evaluate(patched);
assert.deepEqual(fixed.map(view => view.title), ['Parts Tray', 'Example panel', 'OpenAI Developers']);
assert.strictEqual(fixed[0], hosted[0]);
assert.strictEqual(fixed[1], hosted[1]);
console.log('GREEN: patched selector returns three rows and keeps the hosted entries.');

const sameTitle = {hostId: 'local', server: 'codex_apps', title: 'Example panel',
  entrypoint: {type: 'thread'}, tool: {name: 'another_tool', _meta: {_codex_apps:
    {resource_uri: '/another-app/redacted-link/another_tool'}}}};
assert.equal(evaluate(patched, {localViews: [...local, sameTitle]}).filter(
  view => view.title === 'Example panel').length, 2);
console.log('PASS: distinct tools sharing a title remain available.');

const standalone = ['server-a', 'server-b'].map(server => ({hostId: 'local', server,
  title: 'Example panel', entrypoint: {type: 'thread'}, tool: {name: 'open_panel'}}));
assert.equal(evaluate(patched, {localViews: [...local, ...standalone]}).length, 5);
console.log('PASS: independent standalone MCP servers remain available.');

assert.deepEqual(evaluate(patched, {route: 'chatgpt-thread'}).map(view => view.title),
  evaluate(original, {route: 'chatgpt-thread'}).map(view => view.title));
console.log('PASS: ChatGPT route remains unchanged.');

const deniedHosted = evaluate(patched, {permitted: view => !('appId' in view)});
assert.equal(deniedHosted.length, 3);
assert.ok(deniedHosted.every(view => !('appId' in view)));
console.log('PASS: filtering permissions before dedup preserves permitted local fallbacks.');
console.log('All six assertions passed; installed app and repository were unchanged.');
```

Expected output:

```text
RED reproduced: original selector returns five rows for three canonical tools.
GREEN: patched selector returns three rows and keeps the hosted entries.
PASS: distinct tools sharing a title remain available.
PASS: independent standalone MCP servers remain available.
PASS: ChatGPT route remains unchanged.
PASS: filtering permissions before dedup preserves permitted local fallbacks.
All six assertions passed; installed app and repository were unchanged.
```
